From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Sep 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Test the engines floor instead of asserting it

`package.json` declares `engines.node: ">=22"`, and the matrix ran
`24.x` and `latest`, so the floor was never exercised. A floor CI does
not run is a claim, and this package's whole posture is that a claim
nothing checks goes stale: `>=24` stood unexamined until someone noticed
the entire Node surface is three `node:crypto` imports present since
Node 16, against a `target: es2021`.

Adding `22.x` makes the lowest supported version the one the suite
proves. It costs three more matrix cells.

Apply with `git am` from a checkout whose token holds the `workflow`
scope, and delete this file in the applying commit.
---
 .github/workflows/build.yml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/build.yml b/.github/workflows/build.yml
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/build.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/build.yml
@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@ jobs:
       fail-fast: false
       matrix:
         os: [ubuntu-latest, macos-latest, windows-latest]
-        node-version: [24.x, latest]
+        node-version: [22.x, 24.x, latest]
     runs-on: ${{ matrix.os }}
     steps:
       - uses: actions/checkout@v4
-- 
